node_modules/

# Finder / file-delivery duplicates ("foo 2.html"). Never intentional, and on this
# repo a stray .html is a publish risk rather than clutter: GitHub Pages serves main
# directly, so a committed duplicate goes live, and these copies are usually older
# drafts. On 2026-08-25 a `case-studies/fee-recipient-attribution 2.html` still
# carried 0x prose that had been deliberately revised away. The same class recurred
# in the afm repo on 2026-09-08 (`voice_inanimate_subject_audit 2.md`, swept into a
# PR by `git add -A`), which is why both repos now guard it.
#
# Safe here: no tracked file in this repo has a space in its name, so this masks
# nothing real.
#
# It only stops the duplicate being COMMITTED. scripts/publish-gate.js walks the
# filesystem with fs.readdirSync and skips only node_modules and .git, so an ignored
# duplicate still fails a LOCAL gate run. Delete the file; .gitignore will not
# silence the gate.
* [2-9].html
